Chapter 10, Section 16: "Treachery"



"Subaru is—"

"—an Archbishop of Sin?"


It was an accusation that made absolutely no sense.

Even when repeated aloud, as if to confirm it, it still made no sense whatsoever. It was so nonsensical that if their goal was to catch him off guard, it was such a resounding success he could almost laugh.

But—

The grim expression on the giant before him—the man called Marcos—was far too stern to laugh off such an incomprehensible suspicion as a joke.

At the very least, Garfiel, entrusted with the position of the camp’s chief warrior, saw absolutely no option to relax his guard in this man’s presence.

"——"

With a small sniff, Garfiel quietly took in the heavy tension filling the royal residence. What he sensed was restrained fighting spirit, unease and distrust that shook the heart, and hidden behind them, the sharp, pungent stench of fear.

It was an atmosphere he’d had many chances to smell recently in the empire of Vollachia—the air of a fire magic crystal storehouse on the verge of explosion.

In other words—

"You lot... tryin' to pick a fight with us?"

"—Does that mean you're refusing our request?"

"Hah?! You're the ones spoutin' crap first and now you're makin' faces like we're the ones sellin' you a fight!"

"Wait. No snapping at them, Garfiel. Please."

At that, Garfiel, who had been grinding his fangs in irritation and glaring up at the much taller Marcos, was held back by Emilia's words from behind.

With the addition of "please," even Garfiel had no choice but to pull in his horns. To this, Emilia added a "thank you," then lifted her face with firm resolve.

"I'm sorry for our boy. He was just so very surprised he couldn't speak, so he got angry on my behalf instead."

"Then, is Lady Emilia angry as well, like him?"

"That... yes, I suppose so. After being surprised by you asking such a strange thing, I'm feeling very, very bothered inside. I think I'm about to get angry any moment now. But—"

Emilia paused there and placed a hand on her chest. She toyed with the green magic crystal hanging there, as if using its hard sensation to organize her thoughts.

"—even if I threw a tantrum here, it wouldn't improve Subaru's position at all. That would just be me getting angry because I want to be angry. And I think that would be wrong."

"...You say that clearly, looking me in the eye."

"I haven't really spoken much with Sir Marcos since our last talk. I'm like this now—I've become just a little bit stronger than before. And that, too, is thanks to Subaru."

"——"

At Emilia’s reply, unmoved by emotion yet not browbeaten, Marcos narrowed his eyes with an expression that suggested he had some thoughts on the matter.

Meanwhile, listening to Emilia, Garfiel felt the blood that had rushed to his head slowly cooling down again. Yet the tension in his body wouldn't loosen. He wouldn't let it.

"In the first place, this suspicion of yours seems nothing but absurd. Natsuki-san connected to the Witch's Cult? And at the level of an Archbishop? It's not even laughable."

"That's right! Besides, Subaru-sama has solved so many problems caused by the Witch's Cult up until now! He's even defeated Archbishops, saved me and everyone in the village... please don't say such strange things!"

Supporting fire came from Otto and Petra, and Garfiel nodded along with a "Yeah, yeah!"

They had defeated the Archbishops of 'Sloth,' 'Greed,' and even 'Gluttony' in battles led by Subaru, or captured them, dealing a massive blow to the Witch's Cult. In addition, Subaru had contributed greatly to the subjugation of the Three Great Demon Beasts, the 'White Whale' and the 'Great Rabbit.'

The idea that such a Subaru was with the Witch's Cult was just too ridiculous a story.

"Yeah, don't tell me y'mean this mess is 'cause of a big fight 'tween allies. Even if I scrapped with Bro Otto, I wouldn't beat 'im to a pulp. Not that we'd fight in the first place, though."

"I'm not sure if the comparison to Garf and Otto-san is appropriate, but I also find that question perfectly reasonable. ...I can't imagine that man being capable of harboring such malice."

"Yeah, seriously. It's true that bro does tend to take on a mountain of troublesome stuff, but I'd say the biggest reason he does it is 'cause he doesn't think things through, y'know?"

Though there was a slight barb in Rem's comment, the opinion of the camp, including Meili who followed up after her, aligned with Garfiel's. This was their consensus, centered around Emilia.

Receiving this, Marcos's rock-like expression didn't budge in the slightest.

"I understand that the members of the camp place immense trust in the Knight Natsuki Subaru. With that in mind, I must again request that Lady Emilia come to the castle."

"Should I talk about what we just discussed to the people at the castle as well?"

"In addition to that, if you could answer our questions without falsehood. Though it may be meddlesome of me, I will convey that offering your utmost cooperation in resolving this suspicion is the best way to clear the doubt."

"——"

"—Um, may I?"

Just as Emilia's violet eyes lowered thoughtfully under Marcos's repeated demand, it was Rem who spoke up.

Like Garfiel, she was sharply vigilant of the royal soldiers around them as she asked.

Her question was—

"Is the person in question... Natsuki Subaru, not required to be there as well?"

—In that instant, the air among the royal soldiers completely shifted at her question.

"——"

The emotions directed at them changed, sharpening, and Garfiel's hair stood on end.

Physically, no swords were drawn, but the sensation was as if countless sword tips were pointed at them. That scrutiny dominated the reception room of the royal residence. It was like the barely still surface of water being trampled, a ripple of emotion causing persistent, unvanishing waves.

It was a hair-trigger situation where a single bursting bubble, a single droplet, could set everything off—

"—Silence."

With just that one word—no, with the ferocious sword aura that accompanied that single word—he mowed down the swaying emotions of the masses, forcing the waves into submission by sheer power.

"—Gh!"

Garfiel felt an illusion as if struck by a palm as huge as a mountain. In that instant, every pore on his body opened, and he barely suppressed his instinct to partially transform into a beast with sheer reason.

Moments before, his instincts had been set bristling by a sword aura so vastly greater than what the royal soldiers had directed at them, an extraordinary power emanating from its source.

"My soldiers were extremely rude. —And to the warrior over there, I apologize again for the discourtesy."

"—Hah? Only... me?"

"I meant to direct it only at the soldiers, but you were caught in it. I see you are quite well-trained."

At Marcos's silent bow, Garfiel noticed that the other members of his camp looked confused, furrowing their brows with no idea what just happened.

It seemed Marcos was telling the truth; those who had actually felt that were truly only Garfiel and the original targets, the royal soldiers. —Once again, Garfiel was made keenly aware.

Marcos Gildark—hidden in the shadow of the extraordinary ' Sword Saint' Reinhard van Astrea, but the apex of the Kingdom of Lugunica's Knights—his strength was no mere paper tiger.

"...The way you all just reacted felt very, very strange to me. Will you answer Rem's question? How are Subaru and Beatrice doing?"

Leaving Garfiel, with both dread and vigilance in his green eyes, aside, Emilia narrowed her eyes thoughtfully as she questioned him. Marcos deepened the shadows on his face for a moment, then—

"—Lady Emilia, what of the movements of the Knight Natsuki Subaru?"

"Today, he went out saying he had something to discuss with Sir Miklotov. Alone... well, two of them, since Beatrice is with him, but he said he had an appointment to talk, so—"

"—Lord Miklotov McMahon has passed away."

"Eh."

The report, cut in as if interrupting Emilia, had an impact far greater than the rudeness of the interruption itself, sharply striking the air of the reception room.

Naturally, Garfiel knew the name Miklotov McMahon.

Not only because Subaru and the others had gone to meet him, but he was a big name involved in the Royal Selection. A central figure of the 'Council of Elders,' hearing of his death couldn't help but be shocking.

But the real shock was in the words that followed.

As Garfiel and the others remained in stunned confusion, Marcos pressed on relentlessly.

He said—

"Currently, the kingdom is pursuing the whereabouts of the Knight Natsuki Subaru and Duchess Crusch Karsten, who is also a Royal Selection candidate, under the suspicion that they conspired together in the death of Lord McMahon."

"Wait! What do you mean? Subaru, and Lady Crusch? Involved in Sir Miklotov's death...?"

"The sword wounds on Lord McMahon's remains recovered from the scene matched a knight's sword bearing the crest of House Karsten. There are also reports that Lord McMahon fell by the hand of the Duchess of Karsten, and that the Knight Natsuki Subaru aided her escape."

"Wha...!"

Assaulted by the violence of this neatly arranged information, Garfiel felt a momentary dizziness.

Not only had a key figure like Miklotov been killed, but it was supposedly Crusch who did it, and Subaru who helped—it could only be seen as a preposterous false accusation.

"That, that Duchess...!"

Even putting aside the ridiculous suspicion on Subaru, Garfiel couldn't believe that Crusch was suspected of such an atrocity.

Garfiel's contact with Crusch amounted to just a single day and a half in the Watergate City. But she was a comrade who had stood shoulder to shoulder with him in that battle, fighting the Witch's Cult together to save the city.

He knew she was someone who could genuinely swing a sword for the sake of others, and he had truly wanted to do something about the price she had paid for it.

Though Garfiel hadn't witnessed it directly, when he heard Crusch's body had been healed by the power of the 'Dragon Church's' sacrament or whatever, he had cast aside all the various complications surrounding the Royal Selection and felt simply relieved that she was okay.

—So, the idea that this same Crusch committed an atrocity, and Subaru aided her? What a load of nonsense.

"—Allow me to confirm. Saying you are pursuing their whereabouts means that Natsuki-san and Lady Crusch are currently still on the run, correct?"

Suddenly, a question flew out, spoken in a voice that suppressed emotion, aimed at properly grasping the situation. It went without saying that the speaker was Otto, the intellectual core of the camp.

Emilia's violet eyes, still trying to contain her agitation, turned toward Otto.

"Otto-kun..."

"It's an important point. The fact that the Captain of the Royal Guard came here personally is likely for reasons of caution, rather than as a gesture of respect toward Lady Emilia."

"Caution? You mean you think Miss Emilia or we might run wild?"

"That's not impossible, but the primary concern is a rendezvous. It's a deployment made to guard against the possibility of Natsuki-san and the others joining up with us and being hidden. Am I wrong?"

"—Explaining the intent behind our troop deployment involves military secrets, so I cannot answer that."

"I see. Not being denied is sufficient."

At Otto's response to Marcos's reply, as Garfiel desperately tried to knead the surging passion and agitation inside him into something harmless, he felt nothing but reassurance.

At times like this, he truly thought that he was glad Otto was here.

On a complex board where multiple schemes interweave, Garfiel trusted that Otto would sort things out properly and give them the necessary information, allowing him to focus on his role as the shield.

Here, too, Garfiel resolved to carry out that duty without being swayed by unnecessary emotions.

"The death of Lord McMahon, and the suspicion that he is a member of the Witch's Cult... they seem related, yet also not. In light of that, wanting to hear Lady Emilia's story directly seems a bit much, no matter how you look at it..."

"I have already conveyed that the best way to resolve the suspicion is for you to come to the royal castle and answer our questions. Should you refuse this, we will be forced to conclude that Lady Emilia and her camp have abandoned their responsibility to explain regarding the suspicions on the Knight Natsuki Subaru."

"That's basically coercion, regardless of Emilia-neesama's will!"

"It is not coercion. However, should you not comply, the suspicion will remain mere suspicion, and the kingdom will simply decide its stance toward the Knight Natsuki Subaru."

"——"

Without letting emotion into his low voice, Marcos continued his unchanging request.

Push or pull, trying to move the man who sat as solidly as a literal mountain was impossible. An air of frustrated impatience had begun to spread, both on their side and the other, when—

"—Understood. I will go to the castle. I will speak of Subaru there."

"A wise decision."

"...Then, I will get ready right away."

Hating both the stagnation and the potential breakdown of the situation, Emilia decided to comply with their demand. Marcos nodded. With her eyes still harboring antipathy towards his attitude, Petra moved to prepare for going to the castle.

However, "No," Otto stopped Petra. Still with his eyes narrowed, he gave a small nod to the wide-eyed Petra, then—

"We will choose who accompanies her to the castle carefully. ...Isn't that right?"

"You are perceptive. That speeds things along."

"...What do you mean?"

At the crossing glances between Otto and Marcos, Emilia furrowed her shapely brows. To Emilia's question, Marcos straightened his tall back and stated—

"Regarding Lady Emilia's visit to the castle, we cannot permit all members of her camp to accompany her. Currently, the suspicion surrounding the Knight Natsuki Subaru has the potential to extend to Lady Emilia's entire camp. In order to preserve the independence of her testimony, we must limit her attendant to a single person responsible for her personal care."

"A single caretaker, just one...!?"

"We appreciate your understanding, and ask for your cooperation in this inconvenience."

Likely having foreseen their surprise, Marcos's attitude was immovable.

Garfiel glanced at Otto, and from the slight frown on his older brother figure's face, he guessed that Otto had also anticipated this answer. The problem was, even having anticipated it, it was still undeniably a painful blow for the camp.

"At least let me alone..."

"That is not advisable. I understand your desire to serve as an escort as a warrior, but you are more than sufficient as an immediate combat asset. If Lady Emilia, who is at the center of this suspicion, were to come to the castle accompanied by military force, it would be seen not as a defense but as a show of force."

"That's just slander..."

"It means there are those who would perceive it as such."

With every word, the other party kept stifling their intentions. Garfiel wanted to dodge this somehow, but the fact that even Otto wasn't interjecting meant the opponent's logic held water.

But—

"When it comes to a caretaker..."

Given the current state of their camp, the only candidates were Petra and Rem. If Frederica were here, leaving it to her older sister would have been the best option, but that was wishing for the impossible.

Entrusting Emilia to Rem, whose 'memories' had not returned, was difficult, and while sharp-witted, leaving such a monumental situation to Petra was anxiety-inducing.

What on earth was the best course of action—just as he thought that—

"—Then it's settled. Ram will accompany Lady Emilia."

"—Gah, Ram!?"

Saying this, Ram appeared at the entrance to the reception room, and Garfiel's eyes widened.

Seeing Ram, changed into her familiar maid uniform and with her usual strong-willed expression, Garfiel, of course, couldn't hide his surprise, and neither could Emilia and the others.

After all, Ram was supposed to be resting in a state nearly bedridden, due to the heavy workload that began with the journey to the Pleiades Watchtower. She was to stay in the Royal Capital, not accompanying them on the trip to Priestella scheduled for today, and await Garfiel and the others' return.

Yet here she was, on her feet, and what's more, standing regally beside Emilia. Before their dumbfounded faces, she performed a curtsey, lightly pinching the hem of her skirt.

"Apologies for my lateness. I was responsibly checking the softness of the beds and thus was late in noticing our guests' arrival."

"...So the feel of the bed, is it all right now?"

"Indeed. I would deem it passing."

With a small shrug, Ram's expression showed no sign of fatigue. But it was clear this was just her usual skill at hiding her burdens, and not that she had actually recovered. Even that exchange with Emilia just now was Ram substituting her own physical condition with the condition of the bed. There was no doubt that unease remained.

But—

"Nee-sama..."

"Rem, I leave the rest of that leftover group to you. Nothing gets done without the power of the cute and capable Ram and Rem sisters. Petra is slightly better, at least."

"—Yes, understood."

Naturally, at Ram's words as she settled into that role, Rem swallowed her worries and anxieties for her sister and nodded, holding back tears in her pale blue eyes.

Beside that exchange, Garfiel looked toward Otto. This was an action that could even be seen as Ram's unilateral decision, but Otto's judgment was—

"Yes, I believe Ram-san is the right person. Can we entrust Lady Emilia to you?"

"You needn't say it. Otto, you'd best shape up yourself. Garf, try to be used skillfully, at least."

"...Don't need ya t'tell me."

While Emilia, Rem, and even Otto respected Ram's decision and responded resolutely as those entrusted with her words, a hint of weakness crept into Garfiel's voice. Garfiel was ashamed of it, but Ram slightly softened her light pink eyes and,

"Idiot."

She pushed aside Garfiel's weakness with sweet sternness.

"—Everyone, I'm off. I'll properly clear up Subaru's misunderstanding and explain so everyone can understand."

Thus, with the entire camp unanimously agreeing on Ram as the attending caretaker, Emilia solidified her resolve to go to the castle and declared it, looking across the faces of Garfiel and the others.

To be honest, the situation was intolerably unjust.

When the atmosphere is like this, just being on the receiving end unilaterally is a bad sign. If this were a brawl, letting the opponent do whatever they wanted freely would lead to an immediate loss.

To not lose, you have to see through what the opponent wants to do and stop it, and in turn, you have to do what you want to do right back.

"As always, please lend me your strength. Please, I beg of you."

Saying so, Emilia bowed her head deeply, entreating her comrades in the camp.

Even though she's the leader of the camp, a Royal Selection candidate, and holds a properly important title, she still doesn't hesitate to bow her head and rely on the strength of others.

That aspect of her, that is why Garfiel—no, why all their comrades in the camp—feel they want to give their all for Emilia and for Subaru.

That's why—

"Yeah! 'Course! Ain't nothin' t'worry 'bout, Emilia-sama!"

At the very least, to dispel the anxiety of Emilia and Ram heading to the castle, Garfiel raised his fist and shouted in an especially spirited voice.



