And so, after seeing off Emilia—who took only Ram as her attendant—as she was escorted by Marcos and the others to the royal castle, the remaining group...

"Everyone, gather your belongings. Just the bare minimum is fine. —We leave in five minutes."

...Otto quickly announced this to those left behind in the royal residence.

Having chased away the soldiers left to watch the residence, wanting to confer within the camp alone, they had only just been left to themselves in the reception room when this statement came. Garfiel couldn't help but gape.

"Five minutes?! We ain't waitin' for Emilia-sama?!"

"Correct. The situation won't allow for a moment's delay. Both the suspicion placed on Natsuki-san and the forceful insistence on Emilia-sama coming to the castle... the aim is obvious."

"—It's to remove her from the Royal Selection, isn't it."

"Almost certainly so."

Answering both Garfiel's question and Petra's comment, Otto, his usually gentle features now harboring sharp intelligence, raised a finger. "Listen," he began.

"The timing overlaps far too neatly. On the very day he was summoned by Lord McMahon, Natsuki-san gets caught up in a bloody incident... and what's more, the perpetrator is Lady Crusch, a fellow Royal Selection candidate. A significant power is at work here."

"They intend to remove both Emilia-sama and the other candidate from the board together... That man was used for that purpose, wasn't he."

"With the information we currently have, it's the only way to think. Regarding Lady Crusch, her continuation in the Royal Selection was already precarious from the moment she sought help from the Dragon Church..."

"Nee~, I get the discussion's endless and all, but don't we really not have that much tiiime? It'll be bad if that boulder of a man comes back, riiight?"

It was Meili who interjected, calling a halt to the drawn-out conversation. Playing with her braid, her little red scorpion on her head clicking its pincers, she spoke—"that boulder of a man" probably meant Marcos.

Indeed, right now Marcos was accompanying Emilia to the royal castle and was absent from this place. Currently, the royal residence was surrounded by royal soldiers ordered to stand by, effectively placing the remaining Garfiel and others under a form of quiet house arrest, but—

"If we obey quietly, we'll run out of options. We move before Sir Marcos returns."

"...We're going to search for him, then."

"Natsuki-san and Lady Crusch. We can't even begin to form a proper argument unless we know what happened to those two and what they saw at Lord McMahon's estate."

"Is that alright? Relying on him, I mean."

"Even if Natsuki-san fails, Beatrice-chan is with him. The one attached to him is far more reliable than the main body himself."

A small smile flickering across his face, Otto looked at Rem reassuringly. Rem, her brows drawn down in worry, accepted his consideration, though it likely wasn't reassurance from the bottom of her heart.

Within the flow of everyone working to crush that anxiety, Garfiel slapped his own cheeks with both hands.

"Alright! I'll steel my resolve too! Bro Otto, even if we disappear, Emilia-sama and Ram are..."

"There should be no danger to them. Skipping various procedures to inflict harm upon Emilia-sama, a Royal Selection candidate, would not be permitted. They'll abide by that rule. In any case, from the moment they demanded her presence at the castle, their side's goal has been solely to confine Emilia-sama."

"Tch, got it! Then I'll smash every last one of the guards, and in that gap—"

"—We must not."

"Hah?!"

Cracking his knuckles to raise his fighting spirit, Garfiel found Otto shaking his head before him. His momentum thwarted, he stared wide-eyed as Otto looked at him with a serious face.

"The guards are just following orders; they aren't our enemies. We must avoid injuring them. Ideally, we don't even make them draw their swords. What we must do is flee in order to prove our innocence, not start a war."

"If we cause casualties, it will worsen Emilia-sama's and Nee-sama's... and his position."

"That's the gist of it."

As Otto nodded, adjusting his hat, Garfiel ground his back teeth. He understood. He understood the logic. It was logic he understood, but Garfiel couldn't think of any development from there. Of course, if Marcos returned, their chances of safely escaping the royal residence would vanish entirely.

But at least right now, escape was possible through brute force. If that was sealed, what in the world could they do—

"For areas where the watch is thin, I can ask the insects and birds to scout. I can also ask them to create diversions. Though even that isn't foolproof..."

"—In that case, I have an idea."

"Truly, Petra-san?"

At the proposal of Otto's usual method using his divine protection, Rem's eyes widened at Petra, who raised her hand with a jolt. Accepting this, Petra said "Yes!" and clenched her small hands tightly into fists.

"I'm very, very angry right now. At Subaru being suspected, at Emilia-neesama being glared at, and at Ram-neesama being forced to push herself. So, I absolutely refuse to do what they say!"

"That's fearsome an' reliable, but... what're ya gonna do?"

"Of course, a special plan. It's Otto-san's specialty!"

"My... specialty...?"

Thus singled out all of a sudden, Otto tilted his head with a look of utter cluelessness. Meanwhile, Petra, her cheeks flushed with excitement, was brimming with confidence in this so-called plan of hers.

"Petra-chan, what are you planning to do~?"

"It's something Meili-chan and Garf-san both know, too. Listen—"

So saying, Petra beckoned everyone closer, and as they leaned in, she proudly explained the contents of her special plan.

It was—





