"Fire—!!"

A royal soldier's frantic shout rang out, and panic spread like wildfire through the royal residence.

What they witnessed was smoke billowing with tremendous force from the kitchen. Faced with the massive generation of smoke, accompanied by heat and a scorched smell, many of the brave soldiers immediately sprang into action.

They rushed into the kitchen to confirm the source of the fire, urgently trying to identify the cause of the smoke. Depending on the situation, they would extinguish it, aiming to quell both the flames and the panic at once.

However—

"The fire's source is under the floor, and the smoke is because the chimney's been blocked... Putting it out won't be easy."

So said Petra, who had proposed the fire alarm operation and also devised its detailed methods. Listening to the panic unfolding exactly as she intended, she deepened her smile. It was a smile that could generally be called adorable, but seeing it up close, Garfiel couldn't shake a sensation that chilled him to the bone.

Regardless—

"Having setting buildings on fire treated as my specialty, I can't say I'm happy about it, you know!"

Setting aside Otto's complaint, the fire alarm operation was a brilliant success.

Unable to expose an important building like the royal residence—and the individuals under house arrest inside—to danger, the royal soldiers were too occupied dealing with the smoke to pay attention to Garfiel and the others' movements.

During that time—

"Sorry 'bout this, but y'all take a quick nap!"

"Apologies. My grudge... is only equal to one Nee-sama's worth."

"—gh"

Garfiel and Rem each took charge of the two soldiers who, at the very least, hadn't left their post at the back door, choking them out to secure the path. They didn't let them draw their weapons. Fulfilling the condition Otto had given beforehand, Rem and Garfiel exchanged glances and nodded.

Then, together with Otto, Petra, and Meili, they slipped outside the building.

"If we were gonna cause a commotion anyway, I could've just used my mabeast friends to do it however you wanted."

"That alone is absolutely out of the question, Meili-chan. If you called mabeasts and had them rampage, it would just substantiate the suspicions on us. Subaru would be an Archbishop of the Witch's Cult, Emilia-sama is tied to the 'Witch of Envy,' Meili-chan runs wild with mabeasts, and Otto-san sets fire to buildings left and right."

"Regarding that last suspicion, just like the previous mansion, there's counter-evidence that Petra-chan was also present, not just me!"

"Setting aside Otto-nii's disposition for now, I get it."

Flipping the hem of her skirt, Meili shrugged as she ran with quick footsteps.

Still, even with her nonchalant attitude, Garfiel thought that what she'd just said probably came from a sense of frustration that was typical of Meili.

Meili had power. But it was a double-edged sword—one that, if wielded, would also endanger those she wanted to protect. The existence of a blade she couldn't use... was what made her feel that frustration.

"Don't ya worry. I'll put in the work to make up for what ya lack."

Running alongside her, Garfiel patted Meili on the head. Immediately, Meili made a displeased face, glaring at him, and Garfiel clicked his fangs.

"Bro Otto's the ears, I'm the nose, and we'll sniff out the boss somehow. 'Til then, well... support us! Support us! Just be cheerin' us on!"

"Cheering... as in, 'do your best'?"

"That's it. Really, bein' cheered on gives ya strength."

Meili looked doubtful, but it was a sensation Garfiel remembered well.

Just like in Priestella, where he'd been headed, when Garfiel had managed to—however imperfectly—fight against Kurgan of the 'Eight Arms,' who had become a corpse soldier. It was thanks to the younger siblings present there—and to the support of the citizens who, pushed forward by Subaru's speech, held onto hope.

Yes, that was it. Garfiel had won there because of the power of support. And the strength to give that support had existed only because Subaru, of all people, had roused the people.

It was the result of Natsuki Subaru having overwritten the despair prepared by the Witch's Cult with hope.

"That boss of ours... there ain't no way he's an Archbishop...!"

The very thought of doubting him was so absurd it was laughable. But it made Garfiel feel as if the back of the man he respected had been sullied, and he was truly, truly furious.

This wasn't just Priestella. There were many who knew Natsuki Subaru's goodness—those from the 'Sanctuary' where Garfiel had lived with his grandmother and the others, the people of Petra's Arlam Village who had been saved from the Witch's Cult, and further still, those who had challenged the White Whale alongside Subaru.

—And the one who believed in Subaru the strongest among them all was, undoubtedly, Emilia.

According to Otto, the demand for Emilia to come to the castle was aimed at confining her from the very start, and the questioning to clear Subaru's suspicion was nothing more than a pretext.

But even so, if the other side truly had any intention of clearing Subaru's name, there was no one else but Emilia who could pour her whole soul into finding the words for it.

"Damn it all."

Frustrating. Frustrating. Just frustrating. So frustrating he couldn't stop being frustrated, over and over.

Hadn't Subaru worked hard? Hadn't he desperately, single-mindedly worked himself to the bone, wanting to be of use to Emilia whom he'd fallen for, wanting to protect the hearts of everyone with him?

So why wouldn't they listen to the voices of those who knew of Subaru's efforts?

If only they gave them that one chance, they would surely understand.

—That Natsuki Subaru is the coolest, most awesome big brother figure Garfiel is proud of, who struggles with everything he has to make a ridiculously huge ideal come true.

"Garf-nii..."

"—Tch, it ain't nothin'! 'Kurgan took down his enemy even after losin' his arms,' yeah! I ain't got time to mope around either!"

Though he'd meant to cheer up Meili, he was the one getting choked up instead. He blasted that feeling away with a vigorous shout and a snap of his fangs, facing forward. At this, Meili narrowed her eyes slightly and murmured something that, to Garfiel, could only be taken as a compliment:

"You all really are companions of Subaru-nii and Emilia-nee, huh."

"—Otto-san, what do we do from here?"

Behind Garfiel's exchange, Rem ran up alongside Otto, who was at the front, and posed the question.

Receiving it, Otto led Garfiel and the others onward. "This way," he said.

"For now, we need to go into hiding so our trail can't be followed. It won't take long before they realize we've escaped. We want to leave the noble district quickly. I'm borrowing their help for that."

"—. ———. I see."

Choosing shadows and back alleys, Otto led the route after they had dashed out of the royal residence. At the edge of Otto's gaze, familiar insects were creeping and crawling about. At the mention of borrowing their power, Rem merely offered a word of understanding. Garfiel had also been made to suffer in the past, so he had quite unpleasant memories regarding Otto negotiating with insects—mainly Zodd bugs. That said, as an ally, there was no more reliable human, nor insects, to have around.

"If we get caught at a checkpoint, it's over. So—Garfiel!"

"Got it! You two, hang on tight!"

"Kyaaa—"

At Otto's call, Garfiel pulled in Meili and Petra, who were right beside him, scooping each up under one arm. He then kicked against the wall before them—the sturdy rampart wall connecting the capital's noble district and common district—and leaped over it.

It was a wall that should have played an important role in the capital's crime prevention, but with Garfiel's leg strength, it was a simple hop.

"Wait here a bit. Gotta go get Bro Otto and Rem, too."

"I get that... but Garf-san, you can't just suddenly grab girls and pick them up. I was really, really surprised just now."

"Hah? What're y'worryin' 'bout such pointless—don't give me that scary look! I get it, alright!"

Apparently it was serious, as Petra's glare scared him into apologizing. Garfiel then took a running start, glaring up at the wall to leap over it once more—

"—Apologies. We managed to cross without you, Garf."

At those words, Rem landed right in front of him, and Garfiel's eyes widened. More than the fact that she had jumped over this wall, what surprised him even more was—

"Otto-nii managed not to scream, huh."

"It was a close call, though... Rem-san, please put me down. Natsuki-san will kill me for this."

"Huh? Why is his name coming up? I don't understand what you mean."

"That way of phrasing it is exactly how someone who does understand would say it!"

Glared at from close range by Rem, who was holding him up, Otto let out a cry like that. Watching Otto, who somehow managed to get set down on the ground, and Petra teasing him about it, Garfiel let out a long breath, suppressing the surge of emotions he'd felt just moments ago.

Undoubtedly, the situation was bad. Perhaps even worse than when they'd been caught up in the civil war in the Empire.

But surely, Subaru was safe, with Beatrice. Emilia would do her best without overdoing it, as long as Ram was with her. And here with him were Otto, Rem, Petra, and Meili—all reliable. —He would support them.

The situation was bad. But he could still laugh. And if he could laugh, they weren't completely cornered yet.

"Bro Otto, next time I'll carry ya and fly!"

"Yes, please do."

"Yeah. So, what now? We was talkin' 'bout hidin' for a bit."

"Right. First, let me guide us to somewhere uninhabited—"

Slowly shaking his head, Otto had been scanning the surroundings when he suddenly cut off his words. He blinked, then frantically looked at the buildings and shadows near the defensive wall, all around.

Sensing an unmistakable impatience in that, Garfiel spoke up.

"Bro Otto?"

"—They're gone."

"Gone? What's gone..."

"The Zodd bugs. No, not just the Zodd bugs. The other insects I had guiding us here, all of them have vanished completely... It can't be—!"

Eyes widening, Otto turned back—not to the shadows, but to Garfiel and the entire group. His expression rigid, his voice strained with panic, he grabbed Garfiel's arm.

And then—

"I've messed up! Somehow... I've been deceived by the insects!"

"Deceived by insects... you, Otto-san? How is that..."

"It's happening! We've been led here! At this rate, we've got nowhere to run! We need to get out of here immediately—"

The area they had naturally considered a safe zone had been violated. Even Otto, the one directly involved, seemed unable to believe it, yet he was pleading the worst-case possibility to his allies.

Hearing this, Garfiel violently shook off the shock trying to take hold of his heart and moved to act immediately on Otto's words—

"—That's far enough."

—And it was precisely at that moment that nearly the worst possible pursuer caught up with them.

